  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening TVET and Entrepreneurship for the Pharmaceutical and Biotechnological Sector in Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Strengthening TVET and Entrepreneurship for the Pharmaceutical and Biotechnological Sector in Rwanda - The objectives pursued by this special measure action is to to advance country level interventions in Sub-Saharan Africa deemed critical for reinforcing local manufacturing capacities and creating an improved access to health products in Africa. It is a part of Team Europe Initiative on Manufacturing and Access to Vaccines, Medicines and Health Technologies (TEI MAV+) for Sub-Saharan Africa, expanded here to North Africa in collaboration with DG NEAR.The action will support the development of an enabling environment for pharmaceutical products and health technologies in Senegal, Rwanda, Ghana, South Africa, Nigeria and Egypt, with a primary focus on responding to the concrete needs identified at country level, notably skills development, support to the regulatory authority, technology transfers, and ensuring demand for locally produced goods complementing continental and regional level actions. It will also reinforce the dialogue established between Team Europe and these beneficiary countries&#xbf; Governments on this matter.</narrative>
  </description>
